cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "hybrid-inverse-kinematics-solver"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that runs an OpenSim InverseKinematicsSolver over any
  combination of markers, IMU or segment orientations, and prescribed
  coordinates in a single solve, described by one XML setup file. The stock
  OpenSim inverse kinematics tool tracks markers or orientations but not both,
  and cannot prescribe coordinates from an external file alongside them.
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Hambly"
    given-names: "Matthew"
    affiliation: "Griffith University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6258-2558"

repository-code: "https://github.com/PRECISE-research/hybrid-inverse-kinematics-solver"

license: "MIT"

version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-08"

keywords:
  - inverse kinematics
  - OpenSim
  - biomechanics
  - musculoskeletal modelling
  - inertial measurement unit
  - motion capture

# The modelling and the solver itself are OpenSim's work; this tool is a layer
# over them. Cite these alongside the software above.
